WHAT THE DATA IS. 71 mosaic TXM images of 316L stainless steel specimens across
four groups (B2, B3, Wrought, AM/HC) under tension and fatigue loading, stored
as deflate-compressed float32 TIFF and bit-exact to the instrument output.
Pixel-level crack ground truth exists for four images only, all in group B2;
the remaining labels are human corrections and geometric/confirmed-crack-free
negatives of varying provenance. docs/HANDOFF.md section 4 records which is
which and how much to trust each source -- read it before treating any label as
truth.
